# 🌱 EcoTrack - Personal Carbon Footprint Tracker

EcoTrack is a full-stack web application designed to monitor, calculate, and manage personal carbon emissions across daily activities such as travel, food consumption, and energy use. It features AI-powered lifestyle suggestions and comprehensive carbon analytics to promote sustainable living.

---

## 🚀 Live Demo & Deployment
* **Frontend (Netlify):** [View Live App] https://gleaming-profiterole-f84f33.netlify.app/
* **Backend API (Render):** [API Endpoint]https://eco-track-9sdw.onrender.com

---

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

### **Frontend**
* **React.js** (Vite)
* **Tailwind CSS** (for styling & responsive UI)
* **Lucide React** (Icons)

### **Backend & APIs**
* **Python & Flask** (RESTful API architecture)
* **Gunicorn** (WSGI HTTP Server for production)
* **Groq API** (Llama-3.3-70b-versatile for AI-powered eco-recommendations)
* **Carbon Interface API** (Real-world emission factor calculations)

### **Database & Authentication**
* **Firebase Firestore** (Cloud NoSQL Database for user data, habits, and logs)
* **Firebase Authentication** (User management, secure login/signup)

---

## 📊 Key Features
* **Personal Carbon Management Dashboard:** Real-time carbon gauge tracking daily emissions against targeted goals.
* **Category Breakdown:** Detailed tracking of emissions split across Travel, Food (Omnivore/Vegetarian scenarios), and Energy/Solar usage.
* **Daily Habit Logger:** Interactive logging system for user activities and lifestyle tracking.
* **AI Eco Swaps:** Intelligent, AI-generated personalized recommendations powered by the Groq Llama model to reduce carbon impact.
* **History & Analytics:** Visual charts and heatmaps to monitor long-term emission trends.

---

## 📐 Technical Architecture
```text
[ User (Web/Mobile) ]
│
▼ (HTTPS / JSON)
[ Frontend (React + Tailwind CSS) ]
│
▼ (API Requests)
[ Backend (Flask - Python) ] ──► [ Groq API / Carbon Interface / Firebase Auth ]
│
▼ (Read / Write Data)
[ Firebase Firestore Database ]
